# tally 2.2.1 R20 clause 2 (OPERATIONS §2.3): check prints each refused scenario's line in the full-path order of the
# files that declare them (one declared twice, by its first), then each ask refused alone by id, then full path, then
# line.
# P5: one id refused alone in n1/a/s2 and n1/z/s1: a/s2's first. tally 2.2 ordered by scenario id (T's held
# fixture/reviews/same-id-order).
=== options check exit=1
=== model.tally
model plain
  tally 2
  on 2026-03-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2027-12-31
  note "T's base for M3's check fixtures (invented): it loads clean with no warning; each fixture of fixtures.tsv adds files to it"

source card "T's fixture card (invented)"

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

input amt: money PLN

def doubled: money PLN = amt + amt at reader

ask q: doubled law 2026-03-01

version card_2026
  cite card
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  amt = 100.00 PLN "the card"
=== n1/a/s2.tally
scenario s2 over plain
  tally 2
  from 2027-01-01

ask qq: doubled in nowhere_a law 2027-06-01
=== n1/z/s1.tally
scenario s1 over plain
  tally 2
  from 2027-01-01

ask qq: doubled in nowhere_z law 2027-06-01
=== expect
qq: refused: LOAD-SCENARIO ask qq names nowhere_a, neither the model nor a loaded scenario (n1/a/s2.tally:5)
qq: refused: LOAD-SCENARIO ask qq names nowhere_z, neither the model nor a loaded scenario (n1/z/s1.tally:5)
